  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "admission",
      "text": "Students admitted to the major must have Calculus I and Calculus II (or equivalents) and the natural sciences requirement completed with grades of C or higher, a cumulative GPA of 2.80, and completed course evaluations for all transferred courses used for the major. Applications for AOI and other CEAS students are due January 5 (Spring) and June 5 (Fall) and must be made within one year of the first course that applies toward major entry. Non-CEAS students and double major applicants are admitted through a competitive process contingent on program capacity."
    },
    {
      "topic": "advising",
      "text": "Students must complete a specialization. Contact the undergraduate program coordinator and advisor, Elizabeth Petersen (tsm_advising@stonybrook.edu), for advising."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "The Computer Science and Information Systems specializations are mutually exclusive; a student may not specialize in both."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "Applications for major admission follow the process stated in the Admission Requirements section. Intellectual honesty violations ('Q' grade) may cause applications to be tabled."
    },
    {
      "topic": "other",
      "text": "An accelerated BS/MS program in Technological Systems Management exists; see the department website. It is not evaluated here."
    },
    {
      "topic": "sbc",
      "text": "EST 440 and EST 441 partially fulfill the ESI, CER, SPK, WRTD, SBS+, STEM+ and EXP+ SBC categories. Contact the CEAS Undergraduate Student Office for more information."
    }
  ],
